.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH close 1  "close " 
.SH NAME
close \- Close an item, recording why. Closing is final (no hard delete), so a reason is required
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBclose\fR [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Close an item, recording why. Closing is final (no hard delete), so a reason is required
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Closing comment — required: why this item is being closed. `\-` reads it from STDIN
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\-file\fR \fI<REASON_FILE>\fR
Read the closing comment from this file (UTF\-8, verbatim); `\-` reads STDIN. Mutually exclusive with `\-\-reason`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Item id
